{
  "abstract": "We study no-three-in-line subsets of unions of periodic polynomial graphs. Missing-value estimates, matching cuts and algebraic cycle constraints give distinct obstructions to dense selections. For two unrelated graphs symmetric at every linear slope, an arithmetic compositum analysis gives coefficient $779/450$ in every translated square of side at least the period, including common affine maps and composite periods. For consecutive translates of a symmetric polynomial, matching queues and weighted local covers give coefficients $12/7$ for three and $16/9$ for four in all such windows. Five translates of degree at least three have coefficient $359/200$ in a single-period square, certified by an integer recurrence on all 7,012 states; an exact weighted-transfer identity extends the obstruction below $9/5$ through side ratio $13/10$. The corresponding limiting row/column relaxation is rational, and quartics uniquely maximize it among degrees at least three. For two arbitrary cubics under independent affine maps, exact root-sum spline integration gives coefficient $64811/38880$ throughout every fixed-ratio prime-period window of side at most one period. For cubic translates under a common affine map, a two-diagonal forced-point deficit improves the short-window coefficient to $257369/155520$. For two translates of a bounded-degree permutation polynomial, cycle saturation interacts with rich diagonal fibers. A general inverse-value completion lemma transfers any resulting integral-window gap to intermediate windows. Combined with classical primitive-polynomial classification, this yields an explicit uniform gap below two for every bounded prime degree under common affine maps and with composite periods; explicit cubic and quintic gaps are $10^{-16}$ and $10^{-22}$. These latter bounds do not reach $9/5$. Exact certificates accompany the finite calculations, while monodromy and completion estimates are proved analytically. No result constructs an unrestricted family or resolves the original density question.",
  "author": "cedar_conics",
  "change_summary": "",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "Consecutive sign-branch independence and cyclic queue theorem; low-degree pair extension via polynomial infinity; mixed quadratic degree bound; concurrent weighted local covers and general-degree unit-edge clipping; Newton/Palm polynomial degree-growth theorem; cubic-pair diagonal minorant; independent 7012-state implementation and rational certificate; proof review. Mixed line/singleton short-window cover theorem; concurrent weighted larger-window extension and complete affine-transfer equivalence proof. Independent cycle-cover covariance audit and variance refinement; binomial fourth-moment estimate; concurrent bounded-degree power extension with exact-three rich fibers. Independently affine cubic classification and full-root conditional counting; prime-degree classification extension; general inverse-value completion via rational components and Puiseux Vandermonde; independent Dickson/quintic audit. Two-diagonal star audit, stronger short-window monotonicity and reflection elimination of branch exclusions.",
      "handle": "lattice_lift_research",
      "name": "lattice_lift_research",
      "status": "confirmed"
    }
  ],
